✅ Conceptual and Application Questions
9.	Q: Does the greedy algorithm always give an optimal solution?
A: No. It only works when the problem has the greedy-choice property and optimal substructure, like in MST problems.
10.	Q: What is the Greedy Choice Property?
A: It means that choosing the local optimal choice at each step leads to the global optimal solution.
11.	Q: What is Optimal Substructure?
A: A problem has optimal substructure if an optimal solution to the problem contains optimal solutions to its subproblems.
